<title>UK: Williams continues to fall after Chubb bid.</title>
<headline>Williams continues to fall after Chubb bid.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Williams Holdings Plc shares continued to be hit after it launched a 1.3 billion pound bid for security equipment manufacturer Chubb Security on Friday.</p>
<p>By noon it lost 36 pence or 10.65 percent at 302-1/2 pence, on a trading volume touching nearly 14.2 million shares.</p>
<p>The company forecast a 11 percent rise in its 1996 pretax profit at 243 million stg but also said it was seeking a new five-year credit facility for about 1.0 billion stg to help finance Chubb's acquisition.</p>
<p>The takeover of Chubb would creat Williams into a 2.7 billion stg security conglomerate. The global security business is valued at more than 25 billion stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
